⑩00000171⑿
易考范文十四
⑩00000460⑿
Obviously, the picture above depicts an exciting event,
⑩00000995⑿
a milestone in our country's space exploration:
⑩00001390⑿
the first lunar probe of China was launched.
⑩00001749⑿
Named after a Chinese goddess who flew to the moon,
⑩00002065⑿
Chang'e No.1 spreads its wings in the outer space,
⑩00002499⑿
fulfilling the dream of flying to the moon,
⑩00002787⑿
which Chinese people have cherished for thousands of years.
⑩00003181⑿
China has witnessed a giant leap in the outer space research in recent years.
⑩00003739⑿
These achievements will undoubtedly benefit Chinese people,
⑩00004177⑿
even humanity as a whole.
⑩00004391⑿
To begin with, the successful launch of satellites
⑩00004723⑿
and manned spacecraft builds our confidence
⑩00005014⑿
in making more headway in the space exploration.
⑩00005319⑿
Besides, the analysis and exploitation of the useful materials
⑩00005812⑿
beneath the lunar surface will make it possible
⑩00010104⑿
to supplement the natural resources of the globe,
⑩00010417⑿
which are on the verge of being exhausted.
⑩00010677⑿
However, many people are not supportive of space research.
⑩00011122⑿
The enormous amount of money and energy wasted on the project,
⑩00011533⑿
they argue, might have been devoted to those struggling for food and shelter.
⑩00012017⑿
What's more, they are troubled by the idea that
⑩00012354⑿
excessive space exploitation will eventually lead to catastrophe of the world.
⑩00012969⑿
Therefore, they suggest the pace should be slowed down.
⑩00013333⑿
Despite those doubts and hesitations,
⑩00013658⑿
the advantages of the space research far outweigh its disadvantages.
⑩00014138⑿
It will certainly usher in a brighter world for us.
